syntax:
C++ return statements, especially with complex objects:

```c++
MyClass func() {
  MyClass obj; 
  // ... operations on obj
  return obj; // RVO/NRVO may occur here
}

MyClass func2() { return MyClass{}; } // RVO likely
```
The key difference for NRVO is that the returned object has a name in the function. When it does not have a name, like in the second example, the compiler has more leeway in how to optimize.
